    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0205" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg103"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-10-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 15, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1027.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram of September 29
                    last, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy in translation of a note
                    addressed, under date of September 28, 1908, by the Wai-wu Pu to all the <pb
                        facs="0206" n="104" xml:id="pg104"/> foreign representatives in Peking,
                    announcing that all the treaty powers having now signified their assent to the
                    enforcement of regulations prohibiting the importation of morphia and
                    instruments for its injection, such prohibitory regulations will become
                    operative from January 1, 1909.</p>
                <p>I have sent, for their information and guidance, copies of this note to all of
                    our consulates general and consulates in China.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d91-a1.xml" xpointer="d91-a1"/>
            </div>
